uared equals these 36 is  canceled out and we're just left with 36  okay now what I'm going to do is I'm  going to divide everything by 36 because  ellipses we want them to equal one so  I'm just going to divide everything by  36 36 and so you can see this reduces to  X minus 2 squared over 4 and y minus  three squared over 9 equals one so now  it's in the standard form okay for an  ellipse and you can check out my video  on ellipses for graphing and identifying  the key points of ellipses but let's  look at another completing the square  example to put this conic section into  its standard form we've got some larger  numbers here I might have to go to the  calculator to make this a little bit  easier on us but let's do the same thing  let's group the Y's together let's group  the XS together and so on but before we  do that let's analyze what type of conic  section we're working with here so we  notice there's a y squared term and an x  squared term but you see how they have  opposite signs this one's negative this  one's positive that tells us it's a  hyperbola so it's good knowing going in  what type of section we're working with  so let's go ahead and group the Y's  together 16 y squared minus 128 Y okay  I'm going to group the X's together and  I'm going to move the 239 to the other  side so minus 239 same thing we're going  to group these and we're gonna factor  out the leading coefficient this is a  plus in between okay so I'm gonna factor  out the 16 so if I do that that comes  out to Y squared minus and okay let's  see what's 128 divided by 16 let's just  check that real quick okay it's 8 ok so  that's going to be 8y and if we factor  out a negative 1 here we're gonna be  left with x squared minus 2x equals  negative 239 ok so to complete the  square what we're gonna do is we're  gonna take 1/2 of negative 8 which is  negative 4 square it that's 16 but  remember because it's in parentheses  it's actually 16 times 16 that's 256 we  have to add that to the other side you  want to keep that balance the equation  ballots and then here 1/2 of negative 2  is negative 1 negative 1 squared is  positive 1 but really because it's in  parentheses that's a negative 1 so I  have to subtract one from the other side  as well so that comes out to negative  240 and this comes out to  let's see what is that that's 256 so  what is that  that's 16 right okay 16 so now what  we're gonna do is we're gonna factor  this so let's do that we've got Y minus  4 the quantity squared remember is just  half of that middle coefficient we set  it up that way to be a perfect square  trinomial and the same thing here we're  gonna take half of that little  coefficient which is going to be X minus  1 squared K equals 16  with hyperbolas and ellipses you always  want them to equal 1 so to do that I'm  going to divide everything by 16 so it  equals 1 on the right let's just divide  everything by 16 these are gonna cancel  so we end up with Y minus 4 squared  minus X minus 1 squared over 16 this is  over 1 equals 1 so now we're in a  position where we can more easily graph  that hyperbola and analyze it further  check out my video on hyperbolas if you  want to see how to how to graph this one  okay so I hope you're enjoying the  videos if you are you know subscribe to  the channel check out some of my past  videos and I've got some more videos  here coming for you so stay tuned and I  look forward to seeing you in some of  the future videos remember to subscribe  and I'll talk to you soon
 

